          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+functor"} strict functor
            is
            %em amnestic
            if its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain"} domain
            has no more duplication of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphic"} isomorphic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            than its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain"} codomain
          %p
            As ‘amnestic’ is basically a fancy synonym of ‘forgetful’, the idea is to identify a property that one would like in a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
          %p
            For example, the notion of amnestic functors formalizes the sense in which the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+category"} concrete category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Met
                    %mi cont
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Met_cont
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+spaces"} metric spaces
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+maps"} continuous maps
            is often better thought of as the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Met
                  %mi Top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Met Top
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metrizable+topological+spaces"} metrizable topological spaces
            (and
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+maps"} continuous maps
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Met
                  %mi Top
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Met Top \to Set
            has but
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Met
                    %mi cont
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Met_cont \to Set
            does not.
          %p
            There is a corresponding notion of
            %em amnesticization
            of a functor (called the
            %em amnestic modification
            in
            = succeed ")," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+Joy+of+Cats"} The Joy of Cats
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalent+category"} equivalent category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Met
                    %mi cont
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Met_cont \to Set
            produces a category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphic+category"} isomorphic
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Met
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Met Top
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
            (AC) in general to prove that every functor has an amnesticization. Without AC, we can use amnestic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anafunctors"} anafunctors
            to make everything work out, although much of the convenience is lost.
          %p
            Amnesticity is really a property of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+functors"} strict functors
            (or anafunctors) between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+category"} strict
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoids"} groupoids
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            play no role in the definition; only the categories'
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cores"} cores
            matter, and a functor is amnestic iff its core is amnestic. Strict, because the definition requires us to state (in two places) that some isomorphic objects are equal; weakening the definition to follow the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principle+of+equivalence"} principle of equivalence
            leads to a trivial property that every functor satisfies. (That is, up to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              be two
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+categories"} strict categories
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+functor"} strict functor
              from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              is
              %strong amnestic
              if its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+core"} groupoid core
              reflects
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+morphisms"} identity morphisms
            %p
              Explicitly,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              is amnestic iff, for every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi a
                    %mo →
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon a \to b
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              takes to an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+morphism"} identity morphism
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi id
                        %mrow
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi id
                        %mrow
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi b
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(f) = id_{U(a)} = id_{U(b)}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              itself is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+morphism"} identity morphism
            %p
              In other words, a functor is amnestic if its strict
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibers"} fibers
              are
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gaunt+category"} gaunt
          %p
            Observe that this is similar to a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conservative+functor"} conservative functor
          %p
            If we follow the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principle+of+equivalence"} principle of equivalence
            and refuse to state
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equalities"} equalities
            between objects, then we must modify the hypothesis to say that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(a)
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(b)
            are
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphic"} isomorphic
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            (say via
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g\colon U(a) \to U b
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(f)
            is the identity
            %em relative to
            this isomorphism (so
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} id
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi g
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} id
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(f) = \id_{U(b)} \circ g \circ \id_{U(a)}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            be
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(f)
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi a
                    %mo →
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon a \to b
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            are
            %em isomorphic
            (say via
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi a
                    %mo →
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h\colon a \to b
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is the identity
            %em relative to
            this isomorphism (so
            = succeed ");" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} id
                      %mi b
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi h
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} id
                      %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f = \id_b \circ h \circ \id_a
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
            be
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism+of+categories"} isomorphism
          #anafunctor.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Now let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              be two
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+categories"} strict categories
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              be an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anafunctor"} anafunctor
              from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              is
              %strong amnestic
              if its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/core"} core
              reflects
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+morphisms"} identity morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              is amnestic iff, whenever
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
              are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
              is a specification of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              for the anafunctor
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
              is a specification of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
              for the anafunctor
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_\alpha(a)
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi β
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_\beta(b)
              are equal objects in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mrow
                        %mi α
                        %mo ,
                        %mi β
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_{\alpha,\beta}(f)
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+morphism"} identity morphism
              on this object in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
              are equal objects in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is the identity morphism on this object in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
          %p
            We might also demand that
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo =
                    %mi β
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha = \beta
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            is saturated.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                An amnestic
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful functor
                is automatically an
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isocofibration"} isocofibration
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mi D
                        %mo ′
                        %mo =
                        %mi U
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U D' = U D
                %em isomorphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi D
                      %mo ′
                      %mo →
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : D' \to D
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒟
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
                such that
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mi f
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi id
                          %mrow
                            %mi U
                            %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U f = id_{U D}
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi id
                          %mrow
                            %mi U
                            %mi D
                            %mo ′
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi id
                          %mrow
                            %mi U
                            %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f = id_{U D'} = id_{U D}
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                        %mo ′
                        %mo =
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D' = D
            %li
              %p
                An amnestic
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isofibration"} isofibration
                has the following lifting property: for any object
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒟
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
                and any isomorphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %mi U
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : C \to U D
                in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                %em unique
                isomorphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo :
                      %mover
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo →
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde{f} : \tilde{C} \to D
                such that
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mover
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                        %mo =
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \tilde{f} = f
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo ′
                      %mo :
                      %mover
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo ′
                      %mo →
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde{f}' : \tilde{C}' \to D
                were any other isomorphism such that
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mover
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                        %mo ′
                        %mo =
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \tilde{f}' = f
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mover
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo ∘
                        %mover
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                        %mo ′
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi id
                          %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U (\tilde{f}^{-1} \circ \tilde{f}') = id_C
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                        %mo =
                        %mover
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                        %mo ′
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde{f} = \tilde{f}'
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong discrete isofibrations
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isofibrations"} isofibrations
                with discrete fibres.
            %li
              %p
                If the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composite"} composite
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \circ K
                is an amnestic functor, then
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
                is also amnestic.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Most famous
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functors"} forgetful functors
                are amnestic, such as
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Grp
                        %mo →
                        %mi Set
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Grp \to Set
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Top
                        %mo →
                        %mi Set
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top \to Set
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Top
                        %mi Grp
                        %mo →
                        %mi Grp
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top Grp \to Grp
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Top
                        %mi Grp
                        %mo →
                        %mi Top
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top Grp \to Top
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Met
                      %mo →
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Met \to Set
                is amnestic, since the morphisms in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Met"} Met
                are
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/short+maps"} short maps
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Met
                          %mi cont
                        %mo →
                        %mi Set
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Met_cont \to Set
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+maps"} continuous maps
                %em not
                amnestic, as is shown by any set with two different but topologically equivalent metrics (such as
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^2
                with the
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi l
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} l^1
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi l
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} l^\infty
                metrics).
            %li
              %p
                The forgetful functor from a groupoid of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structured+sets"} structured sets
                is amnestic. The examples above may all be defined by starting from such a groupoid and specifying which functions preserve the structure (and so are morphisms in the category of structured sets). So long as this produces no additional isomorphisms, the forgetful functor will be amnestic. But in the case of
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Met
                          %mi cont
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Met_cont
            %li
              %p
                Any strictly
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monadic+functor"} monadic functor
                is amnestic. Conversely, any monadic functor that is also an amnestic isofibration is necessarily strictly monadic.
